diff --git a/docs/design.md b/docs/design.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..caeed94
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/design.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# Design: pre-generated message ids and persisted flag for chat turns
+
+## Goal
+- Clients learn the ids of both messages of a turn from the first SSE event, not only at the end.
+- The final `done` event reports whether the turn was saved, so a failed save needs no separate `error` event.
+
+## Scope
+Included:
+- `ChatSession` gets two ids at creation, exposed as `user_message_id` / `assistant_message_id`.
+- `build_turn_messages` takes the ids instead of generating them.
+- `conversation` event carries `message_id`; `done` carries `message_id`, `persisted`, `created_at`.
+- `ChatTurnResult` gains `user_message_id`, `assistant_message_id`, `created_at`.
+- Remove `EventType.ERROR`, `ProgressEvent.error`, `ErrorCode.PERSIST_FAILED`, `PERSIST_FAILED_MESSAGE`.
+- CLI `_render` prints `!! Không lưu được lượt hội thoại này.` to stderr when a `done` event has `persisted` false.
+- README SSE description updated.
+
+Unchanged: persistence schema, repository ports, agent graph/runner, HTTP endpoints and their paths,
+`ChatTurnResult.message_id` (still `None` when save fails), `persisted`, answer delivery on save failure.
+
+## Interfaces
+- `build_turn_messages(*, conversation_id, user_message_id: str, assistant_message_id: str, run, answer_text, citations, phases, now) -> tuple[Message, Message]`
+- Ids are generated in `ChatService.open_turn` via `new_id()` (two calls) and passed to `ChatSession.__init__`
+  as keyword arguments `user_message_id`, `assistant_message_id`; properties
+  `ChatSession.user_message_id -> str`, `ChatSession.assistant_message_id -> str` (read-only).
+- Events:
+  - `conversation`: `{conversation_id, title, created, message_id}`.
+  - `done`: runner data plus `{conversation_id, message_id: str | None, persisted: bool, created_at: str (ISO)}`.
+- `ChatTurnResult`: adds `user_message_id: str`, `assistant_message_id: str`, `created_at: datetime`.
+- `cli._render(event, evidence)`: new `done` branch.
+
+## Approach
+`new_id()` stays in the domain shared module; the application layer (`ChatService.open_turn`) decides ids,
+making them known before the stream starts. `ChatSession._persist` passes them into the domain builder.
+`done` is always the last event; `persisted` replaces the trailing `error`. `done.message_id` stays `None`
+on failure (the message does not exist), while `assistant_message_id` on the result/session still holds the
+reserved id. `created_at` comes from the built assistant message, so it is reported even on failure.
+The CLI runs the runner directly (no session), so its `done` events lack `persisted`; only an explicit
+`False` triggers the warning.
+
+## Testing
+- Domain: `build_turn_messages` uses the given ids.
+- Service: distinct ids exposed by session; first event and `done` carry them; `created_at` equals stored message;
+  failed save yields `done` last with `persisted` False, `message_id` None, no `error` event; `EventType` has no `error`.
+- CLI: `_render` stderr output for `persisted` false/true.
+- Full suite: `uv run pytest` in `backend/`.
